 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public authorities law, in relation to the process for\nfilling vacancies on the Long Island rail road commuter's council",
    "basePrintNo": "S5164",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5164-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 31,
       "fullName": "Robert Jackson",
       "imgName": "1050_Robert_Jackson.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 1230,
       "sessionMemberId": 2348,
       "sessionYear": 2025,
       "shortName": "JACKSON"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1266-d, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5164\n\nSPONSOR: COMRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public authorities law, in relation to the process\nfor filling vacancies on the Long Island rail road commuter's council\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo reduce the number of names a county executive is required to submit\nto fill a vacancy on the Long Island Rail Road Commuter Council from\nthree to one.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends section 1266-D of the public authorities law to reduce\nthe number of names required to be submitted in order to fill a vacancy\non the Long Island Rail Road Commuter Council.\n\nSection two is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nUnlike the New York City Transit Authority Advisory Council and Metro-\nNorth Railroad Commuter Council (S 1204-e and § 1266-e respectively)\nvacancies on the Long Island Rail Road Commuter Council (LIRRCC) are\nrequired to be filled from a list of three names. This unique, onerous\nrequirement has made filling vacancies unnecessarily cumbersome for\nrecommending elected officials.\n\nAs more and more vacancies have accumulated, it has become progressively\nmore difficult for the council to achieve a quorum, represent the needs\nof commuters, and conduct business. Bringing this aspect of the LIRRCC's\nauthorizing legislation into agreement with that of the New York City\nTransit Authority Advisory Council and Metro-North Railroad Commuter\nCouncil will resolve these issues, ensuring representatives from all\nareas of the Long Island Rail Road's service territory are present when\nthe committee conducts official business, including but not limited to\nelecting a chair and MTA board member.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2024: S8927 Comrie/ A9915 Solages\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:  None.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
